              "category": "COMMITTED"
            },
            "hardDependencies": []
          }
        ],
        "decisions": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The learner already explains voltage and current, so conceptual relearning is not the primary need.",
            "The accepted taught repertoire includes at least node-voltage, mesh-current, superposition, and Thevenin/Norton; no advanced method beyond that repertoire is assumed."
          ],
          "tradeOffs": [
            "No separate conceptual relearning block is scheduled because the reported weakness is method selection, not voltage/current explanation.",
            "No second full practice set or mandatory re-solve of already verified items is scheduled; further remediation is contingent on a concrete observed failure in the integrated task."
          ],
          "unresolvedUncertainty": [
            "The exact course method repertoire is not fully enumerated; the activity uses only methods the learner confirms were taught."
          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop when the changed unfamiliar circuit is solved correctly with a valid selection reason and no assistance.",
            "If the changed circuit is solved correctly, do not add a second check or repeated set."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "sharedDependencies": [],
  "tradeOffExplanation": "The plan spends its effort on the reported weakness, method selection on unfamiliar circuits, rather than on relearning voltage and current or on a second full practice set. This sacrifices broad coverage of every circuit topic in favor of one integrated selection-and-application task with an independent changed circuit. Further remediation is left contingent on a concrete observed failure so the learner is not given unnecessary repeated work."
}

